d 'EQUAIDS': module to estimate AIDS and QUAIDS demand systems with survey data
d
d  equaids estimates the almost ideal demand system (Deaton and
d Muellbauer 1980) and its quadratic extension (Banks, Blundell and
d Lewbel 1997), with demographics by Ray's scaling, by iterated
d feasible generalized nonlinear least squares (Gauss-Newton with
d an analytic Jacobian, in Mata). It reports the elasticities of
d the households (the mean of the household elasticities, the
d default), of the individuals (weights times household size), of
d the market (aggregate) and of a reference household (at the
d means), all with analytic standard errors from the exact
d influence function of the whole procedure: robust, by cluster or
d by survey design (svyset), or a bootstrap of the whole procedure.
d The missing prices of the non-buyers are filled by group means
d (pimpute), and the non-buyers are corrected for by the two-step
d method of Shonkwiler and Yen (1999) (selection), with the probits
d and the imputation in the standard errors. equaidsdiag and estat
d diagnostics check the data and the fit; estat engel gives the
d Engel curves; tables with significance stars can be written to
d Word, LaTeX, Excel, CSV or Markdown; a dialog box and help
d examples run from clickable links are included. A technical note
d documents the model, the estimator and the validation of the
d standard errors; it is included as an ancillary file
d (equaids_technical_note.pdf). 
d
d KW: demand system
d KW: AIDS
d KW: QUAIDS
d KW: price elasticities
d KW: household survey
d KW: censoring
d KW: survey design
d
d Requires: Stata version 14.2
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261003
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar,  Universite Laval 
d Support: email aabd@@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
f equaids.ado
f equaids.dlg
f equaids.sthlp
f equaidsdiag.ado
f equaidsdiag.sthlp
f ../_/_equaids_pimpute.ado
f ../_/_equaids_tabstars.ado
f equaids_estat.ado
f equaids_examples.ado
f equaids_nonbuyers.dta
f equaids_technical_note.pdf
f mexico_2014_cereals.dta
